From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Szabo <szotyesz@Mac.home>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 08:51:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: Skip the invalidation when an RWX interval becomes
 execute-only.

Writes to an RWX page that has compiled code trap and invalidate it, so
when the page is made execute-only again its compiled code already
matches memory and nothing can write it any more. Anti-tamper code that
makes a page RWX, patches it and makes it execute-only again paid for a
second invalidation of every thread's caches on each patch.

Downstream MacNeutron patch, not for upstream FEX, which does not accept
AI-generated code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
index 155403d..b9e1af2 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
@@ -57,6 +57,14 @@ void InvalidationTracker::HandleMemoryProtectionNotification(uint64_t Address, u
     const bool EffectiveRWX = EffectiveExec && ProtIsWritable(Prot);
 
     if (EffectiveExec) {
+      // MacNeutron: an RWX interval made execute-only again needs no invalidation. Writes to an RWX page that has
+      // compiled code trap and invalidate it, so code compiled from it matches memory, and nothing can write it now.
+      // Anti-tamper code that patches a page between two such changes otherwise pays for two invalidations a patch.
+      if (!EffectiveRWX && !(DEPDisabled && !HasExec) && XIntervals.Query(AlignedBase).Enclosed &&
+          RWXIntervals.Query(AlignedBase).Enclosed && RWXIntervals.Query(AlignedBase).Size >= AlignedSize &&
+          XIntervals.Query(AlignedBase).Size >= AlignedSize) {
+        return false;
+      }
       XIntervals.Insert(ProtInterval);
       if (EffectiveRWX) {
         LogMan::Msg::DFmt("Add SMC interval: {:X} - {:X}", AlignedBase, AlignedBase + AlignedSize);
